   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing by tracing the peptide backbone residue by residue. Two features are uncertain: the length of the alkyl linker in the urea bridge and the stereochemistry I assigned from the wedges and hashes.\n\n**Sequence.** Reading from the C-terminal glycinamide, the residues are:\n- Gly-NH2\n- Cys, whose side-chain sulfur is alkylated by the acetyl group (CH2C(=O)) that acylates the Tyr nitrogen, closing the thioether macrocycle\n- Leu\n- N-Me-norleucine, then a second N-Me-norleucine (both with n-butyl side chains)\n- Trp whose indole N1 carries CH2COOH\n- Dab (2,4-diaminobutyric acid), whose side-chain NH is part of a urea\n- Trp\n- 4-hydroxyproline\n- Val\n- Dap (2,3-diaminopropionic acid), whose side-chain NH is part of a second urea\n- Pro\n- Asn\n- N-Me-Ala\n- Tyr\n\n**Urea bridge.** The Dab side chain is NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013(CH2)n\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013CH2 on the Dap. I counted n = 6 from the zigzag. The lower right of the chain is ambiguous in the drawing, so n = 6 is my best reading.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** From the wedges and hashes, the \u03b1-carbons come out in the L configuration, including the proline and hydroxyproline \u03b1-carbons. The hydroxyproline C4\u2013OH is assigned from its hashed bond.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H](N%10)CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N1CCC[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CNC(=O)NCCCCCCN%11)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCNC%11=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1cn(CC(=O)O)c2ccccc12)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCCC)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCCC)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)%10"
